**The unifying diagnosis (the key result):** All 5 remaining cells — **dir_reuse@16, dlm_scaling@32, cache_coherency@32, crash_consistency@32, dir_reuse@32** — reduce to **one root: a 32-node cold inode-cluster read-storm** (root + `.dlm_scaling` inodes in AG0 are force-evicted, then re-read cold, saturating the shared iSCSI target). Confirmed empirically: coherency tests that *don't* drop_caches pass 32/32; the drop_caches-heavy ones timeout.

